    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d694">

                <pb facs="0751" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2—1549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-23T13:00:00-05:00">February 23,
                            1949—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>336. For Cabot and Parker from State &amp; Treas. State and Treas do not consider
                    that present conditions in China warrant grant or loan to China for purposes
                    outlined urtel 550. For your background information <pb facs="0752" n="742"
                        xml:id="pg742"/> only considerations which led to Secy Marshall’s<anchor
                        n="21" xml:id="d694-f1"/> expression of views on use of silver before House
                    Foreign Affairs Committee on Feb 20, 1948,<anchor n="22" xml:id="d694-f2"/>
                    expanded statement subsequently submitted to committee<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d694-f3"/> and airpouched Emb Depins 165 Aug 13, 1948 to
                        Nanking<anchor n="24" xml:id="d694-f4"/> and Secy Snyder’s<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d694-f5"/> views expressed in letter Aug 30, 1947 to Secy
                        Marshall<anchor n="26" xml:id="d694-f6"/> transmitted to Emb as Airgram No.
                    138 of Sept 9, 1947<anchor n="24" xml:id="d694-f7"/> appear to be equally
                    applicable even to limited operation of type outlined reftel. No encouragement
                    should be given to Chinese Govt silver proposal. [State and Treasury.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
